id: pmc-1vma
title: Pending release windows must not claim a never-released package version
description: "Since 2026.8.30 (PR #170), --all-release-tags treats an untagged package.json version as a pending release, puts its window first, and suppresses the leading Unreleased window. That is correct only when a release is actually being cut; resolvePendingReleaseTag derives pending purely from package.json, so in a repo whose version has never been released or tagged the version is a placeholder and the changelog fabricates a heading asserting a release that never happened. Measured: fleet/pm-vcs (version 2026.7.30, zero release tags, never published) and fleet/pm-rl (2026.7.31, same) both regenerate '## Unreleased' as '## 2026.7.30 - 2026-07-30' / '## 2026.7.31 - 2026-07-31'; their Dependency Refresh workflow fails on it (unbraind/pm-vcs run 33379641902). Bisected with the pm CLI held constant: 2026.8.29 good, 2026.8.30/31 bad; the 19 fleet repos whose package version matches a real tag are unaffected. Fix: add an additive --no-pending-release CLI flag and a pendingRelease option on resolveReleaseTagWindows that suppress the fabricated pending window and restore the leading Unreleased window, with default behaviour unchanged."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-31T10:39:11.702Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-02T11:10:05.784Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-02T11:10:05.320Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-02T11:10:05.320Z"
author: pi-agent
resolution: "Added the additive --no-pending-release flag and pendingRelease option; callers can suppress a fabricated pending window while the explicit includeUnreleased:false opt-out remains authoritative."
expected_result: A never-released package version does not fabricate a release heading when suppression is requested; Unreleased appears only when includeUnreleased is enabled.
actual_result: "With includeUnreleased enabled, suppression restores the leading Unreleased window. With includeUnreleased:false, suppression returns no Unreleased window. Default and release-run behavior remains unchanged."
comments[2]:
  - created_at: "2026-08-31T10:43:17.549Z"
    author: pi-agent
    text: "Implemented the additive control: a pendingRelease option on resolveReleaseTagWindows (ReleaseTagHistoryOptions) and a --no-pending-release CLI flag. When the caller asserts nothing is being released, the fabricated pending window is suppressed and the leading Unreleased window restored; with zero release tags the Unreleased window is open-ended so no version fallback can fabricate a heading. Default behaviour is unchanged: pendingRelease defaults to true, and the flag is a no-op when the version is already tagged. The linked test entries record commands and intent; broad quantitative claims about fleet-wide counts, full coverage, blanket revert-proofing, and byte-identical fleet regeneration are not re-asserted here as executed fact (see actual_result for the narrowing rationale)."
    edited_at: "2026-09-01T07:08:19.849Z"
  - created_at: "2026-09-02T11:10:04.815Z"
    author: codex
    text: "CodeRabbit review correction on PR #174: qualified the restoration claim. A leading Unreleased window is restored only when includeUnreleased is not false; the explicit includeUnreleased:false opt-out continues to return no Unreleased window."
